---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { shortHash } from '../site/chain-data';
import { assetMime, getAssetViews } from '../site/assets-view';
// `.card`, `.card-top`, `.hash`, `.num`, `.silent` and the `.tokens` rules all
// live in chain.css — imported here for the same reason every other route
// imports the styles it renders, so this page cannot ship unstyled.
// `.page-head` is in base.css, which `Base.astro` always loads.
import '../styles/chain.css';

/**
 * §3.2b — every file a post references, minted as a token.
 *
 * This exists for **integrity, not theme**. Without it, verifying a post proves
 * its words are untampered while its diagrams are unchecked: someone could swap
 * a published figure and `/verify` would still report a clean chain. The
 * registry closes that, because a post's canonical form carries the sorted
 * hashes of the files it references.
 *
 * Real fields only (§3.2b): hash, token id, mint block, minter, byte size,
 * media type, and the posts that reference it. Transfer history, price,
 * rarity, editions and a marketplace are named in the spec as things this does
 * **not** have — they have no referent on a personal blog, and inventing them
 * is the gimmick creep §1 rules out. There is nothing on `AssetView` that could
 * carry one.
 *
 * A list, so every hash is middle-truncated (§3.1): the full 64 digits belong
 * on the token's own page, where a reader checks them.
 *
 * The empty registry is the ordinary state, not an edge case — `content/assets/`
 * ships with nothing but a `.gitkeep`, and the live chain has minted no token
 * at all. It gets a sentence of its own rather than a blank card, so the page
 * reads as "nothing has been minted" instead of as a page that failed to load.
 *
 * That sentence says **no token has been minted yet**, and deliberately not
 * "no post references a file in content/assets/". A token is minted when the
 * block holding the post *seals*, so a repository whose current month is open
 * is serving referenced images at real urls with an empty registry — the state
 * a working repository spends most of its life in. The old wording was false in
 * exactly that state, and the build printed `copied 1 committed asset file(s)`
 * on the way to rendering it.
 *
 * No clock (§14): `getAssetViews()` reads the registry and the files on disk.
 */
const views = await getAssetViews();
const rows = views.map((view) => ({
  view,
  short: shortHash(view.hash),
  // §14 — re-derived from a file that hashes to the token, or absent. Never
  // `view.bytes` or `view.mime`: the registry's copies of both are covered by
  // no hash on the chain (see the module doc on `src/site/assets-view.ts`).
  mime: assetMime(view),
}));
---

<Base title="Assets — Blogchain" description="Mọi tệp một bài viết tham chiếu, đúc thành token.">
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Assets</h1>
    <span class="sub"><span class="num">{views.length}</span> token</span>
  </div>

  <article class="card" aria-label="Assets">
    <div class="card-top">
      <span class="per">Tệp đã đúc token</span>
    </div>
    <p class="token-note">
      Mỗi tệp mà một bài viết tham chiếu đều được <strong>băm theo byte thô</strong> và đúc thành
      token khi khối chứa bài viết ấy được niêm phong. Nhờ vậy, kiểm chứng một bài viết là kiểm
      chứng cả hình trong bài: đổi một tấm hình đã đăng sẽ làm hỏng hash của giao dịch chứa nó.
    </p>
    {rows.length > 0 ? (
      <ul class="tokens">
        {rows.map(({ view, short, mime }) => (
          <li>
            <span class="id">#{view.tokenId}</span>
            <h2 class="f"><a href={`/asset/${view.tokenId}`}>{view.file}</a></h2>
            <span class="g">
              <span class="hash">{short}</span>
              {' · khối '}<a href={`/block/${view.mintedIn}`}>#{view.mintedIn}</a>
              {' · '}
              {/* An em dash, never the recorded size — the same rule the open
                  block's unverifiable gas figure is under. */}
              {view.bytesOnDisk === null
                ? '—'
                : <Fragment><span class="num">{view.bytesOnDisk}</span> byte</Fragment>}
              {' · '}{mime ?? '—'}
              {view.current ? null : <Fragment>{' · '}<span class="stale">tệp không khớp</span></Fragment>}
            </span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    ) : (
      <p class="silent">
        Chưa có token nào được đúc. Token chỉ sinh ra khi khối chứa bài viết tham chiếu tệp được
        niêm phong, nên tệp trong bài thuộc khối đang mở vẫn chưa có token của riêng nó.
      </p>
    )}
  </article>
</Base>
